{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2020",
    "useDefineForClassFields": true,
    "lib": ["ES2020", "DOM", "DOM.Iterable"],
    "module": "ESNext",
    "skipLibCheck": true,

    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "allowImportingTsExtensions": true,
    "isolatedModules": true,
    "moduleDetection": "force",
    "noEmit": true,
    "jsx": "react-jsx",

    "baseUrl": ".",
    "paths": { "@/*": ["./src/*"] },

    // ON.
    //
    // It was off, and that hid a real bug: `const { show } = useToast()` in
    // seven files, where useToast returns a FUNCTION. Every call was
    // `undefined is not a function` at runtime.
    //
    // Worth knowing WHY it hid for so long: `tsc --noEmit` on this
    // solution-style config (files: [], references: [...]) checks NOTHING. It
    // resolves zero files and reports success. The command that actually runs
    // the check is `tsc -b --noEmit`, which is now `npm run typecheck` and part
    // of `npm run build`.
    //
    // A green check that checks nothing is worse than no check, because it is
    // believed.
    // (remainder of the original note follows)
    // Originally: kept off so you are not fighting the compiler while the errors will make sense.
    "strict": true,
    "noUnusedLocals": false,
    "noUnusedParameters": false,
    "noFallthroughCasesInSwitch": true
  },
  "include": ["src"]
}
